.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt SH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sh
.Nd BusyBox ash shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl il
.Op Fl Cabefmnuvx | Cm +Cabefmnuvx
.Op Fl o Ar option | Cm +o Ar option
.Ar ...
.Oo
.Fl c Ar script Op Ar arg0 args
.No \&| Ar file args
.No \&| Fl s Ar args
.Oc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This page describes BusyBox 1.36.1 ash as built for Rach2.
On os-real, the metal disk and recovery,
.Pa /bin/sh
and
.Pa /bin/busybox
contain the same program; os-simple and the test image install
.Xr ish 1
as their shell instead.
.Pp
The shell is a login shell when
.Ql argv[0]
begins with
.Ql - ,
as arranged by
.Xr login 1
and login-mode
.Xr su 1 .
A login shell reads
.Pa /etc/profile .
The staged profile exports
.Ev PATH
as
.Ql /bin:/usr/bin ,
defaults
.Ev HOME
to
.Pa /root ,
and changes directory with
.Ql cd \(dq$HOME\(dq .
.Pp
This build includes job control, aliases,
.Ev RANDOM ,
prompt expansion, the
.Ev TMOUT
idle timeout, mail checking, and the builtins
.Ic echo ,
.Ic printf ,
.Ic test ,
.Ic sleep ,
.Ic help ,
.Ic getopts ,
and
.Ic command .
The
.Ic sleep
builtin accepts fractional seconds.
Arithmetic is 64-bit and supports bases.
The build also includes some bash compatibility, a command-not-found
hook, history with a size limit, and embedded scripts.
.Pp
Standalone shell support allows an applet to run by name without an
entry in
.Pa /bin .
This is how most BusyBox commands are reached on os-real, whose
.Pa /bin
contains only programs selected by the image manifest.
.Pp
The kernel's lack of threads and dynamic linking does not restrict the
shell's operation.
The
.Ic ulimit
builtin uses the kernel's three resource limits:
.Ql nproc ,
.Ql nofile ,
and
.Ql as .
See
.Xr limits 7 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/profile
.It Pa /etc/profile
System login profile.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl sh -c 'echo $((1 + 2))'
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr limits 7
